{
  "_why": [
    "The sets behind the numbers in this branch's commit messages, in the tree so",
    "they can be re-run rather than believed.",
    "",
    "Written under the rule adopted 2026-08-18: if a commit message states a",
    "measurement, the set it was measured against must be in the tree. Three claims",
    "on this branch were checked by a critic and could not be, because the sets lived",
    "in scratch files: '5/5 real shapes', '9/9 real credentials still caught', and",
    "'the two cases that exposed it are in the test set' — the last of which was",
    "false, neither string existed anywhere.",
    "",
    "Two of those numbers were quoted to Raffael, so the cost was not only that",
    "nobody could re-run them: a number reached a person who could not check it.",
    "",
    "Run with: node tools/measure-gates.mjs <path-to-a-checkout>",
    "It takes a path so the same sets run against main and a branch in one session,",
    "which is what makes a before-and-after honest rather than a claim about the new",
    "side alone."
  ],
